---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="MarioLM — Experiential World Modeling"
  description="MarioLM unifies long-horizon evaluation, optimization, latent user-state modeling, and persistent experiential worlds."
  active="systems"
>
  <main id="main">
    <section class="project-page-hero">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="index-label">Flagship system / 2026</p>
        <h1>Evaluation becomes<br />an experiential world.</h1>
        <p>MarioLM models not only what an AI says, but what its response changes: latent user state, future events, trust, and agency across a temporally continuous interaction.</p>
        <div class="hero-links"><a class="action action-light" href="#architecture">Inspect the architecture</a><a class="action action-outline" href="mailto:xuanmingdi.zxm@alibaba-inc.com?subject=MarioLM%20research">Discuss the research ↗</a></div>
      </div>
      <dl class="project-facts" data-reveal>
        <div><dt>Research support</dt><dd>Thinking Machines Lab</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Annotated turns</dt><dd>500+</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Human agreement</dt><dd>92.3–98.8%</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Rubric depth</dt><dd>L1–L6</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="project-sequence" id="architecture" aria-labelledby="architecture-title">
      <header data-reveal><p class="index-label">Architecture / Evaluation → optimization → world</p><h2 id="architecture-title">One trajectory.<br />Three jobs.</h2></header>
      <ol class="sequence-list" data-reveal>
        <li><span>01</span><h3>MarioEval reads the whole interaction.</h3><p>Scene, latent state, and event-chain signals are evaluated through L1–L6 cascaded rubrics and user-interest-aware halting. The result separates style, persona, drift, and agency rather than collapsing the trajectory into one score.</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><h3>MarioOpt converts failure into learning signal.</h3><p>Hierarchical Reward Decomposition constructs curriculum-shaped rewards; Experience-Focused Policy Optimization returns to the moment where a trajectory starts to fail and repairs it using faithful user simulators.</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><h3>The world preserves consequences.</h3><p>Actions update latent states, future events, trust, and available choices. Evaluation, simulation, and optimization become one persistent environment rather than three disconnected pipelines.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <SiteFooter />
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
